WEBVTT

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:05.200
Gather in the meeting room. There's 
something we need to discuss.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:09.540
It's an important matter that has 
to do with all of your futures.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:48.950
<b>The Overflowing Water</b>

00:01:43.290 --> 00:01:45.860
The reason we had you gather here

00:01:45.860 --> 00:01:47.350
is the pair annihilation phenomenon

00:01:47.350 --> 00:01:48.960
that came up in discussion 
the other day.

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:50.620
Pair annihilation?

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:51.960
What's that?

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:01.420
The other day, the card 
user of The Lovers,

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:03.600
who belonged to the Moscow branch

00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:04.850
of Sefiro Fiore, was annihilated.

00:02:05.860 --> 00:02:07.020
Annihilated?

00:02:07.020 --> 00:02:09.770
As the word suggests, she disappeared.

00:02:10.740 --> 00:02:12.490
The user of The Lovers card

00:02:12.490 --> 00:02:16.150
fought a Daemonia that used 
the same card as its body

00:02:16.810 --> 00:02:18.240
and they were annihilated.

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:23.040
The Elemental Tarot cards 
that we 22 possess...

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:27.830
We explained before that 
they originate from

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:31.500
the same set of Tarot 
cards as the Daemonia.

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:33.250
The Aeon Tarot...

00:02:33.550 --> 00:02:36.990
Right. Because of that, the 
affinity between the tarot cards

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:40.320
used by the Daemonia and the tarot 
cards used by us is rather high.

00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:43.260
And that's why we can use 
the cards to exterminate them.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:47.400
But, with The Lovers card 
disappearing this time,

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:49.940
we have confirmed a certain risk.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:51.440
A risk?

00:02:51.440 --> 00:02:53.210
The fact that it is possible to make

00:02:53.770 --> 00:02:56.320
both of their powers, 
as well as their existence, disappear.

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:00.820
What does that mean?

00:03:01.080 --> 00:03:05.330
For example, if I were to 
encounter the Daemonia

00:03:05.330 --> 00:03:09.420
with my pair annihilation 
phenomenon card,

00:03:09.420 --> 00:03:11.040
The World, fight it, and win...

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:19.050
As a result, everything of that 
Daemonia will disappear, as will I.

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:21.470
But...

00:03:21.470 --> 00:03:24.020
They originally came 
from the same card.

00:03:24.020 --> 00:03:28.890
So if one disappears, the other one 
will as well, to put it simply.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:30.680
But why, all of a sudden...

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:33.500
Yeah, there should have 
been a chance that we

00:03:33.500 --> 00:03:34.940
would have encountered them by now.

00:03:34.940 --> 00:03:37.060
This is speculation, but

00:03:37.060 --> 00:03:39.840
the Daemonia may have purposely been

00:03:39.840 --> 00:03:42.910
avoiding encountering us 
 to protect themselves.

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:48.310
The Daemonia enter a 
person's heart like a virus,

00:03:48.310 --> 00:03:51.870
and divide like cells to spread, 
and it was thought that there were no

00:03:51.870 --> 00:03:55.630
differences in status between the 
victims they spread to.

00:03:55.810 --> 00:03:58.600
But we've learned that
 the counterpart card

00:03:58.600 --> 00:04:00.380
is the source of the others.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:03.660
Meaning, if we don't make our 
counterpart card disappear,

00:04:03.660 --> 00:04:05.080
the Daemonia won't disappear either.

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:07.390
So then all the fighting 
we've done up until now

00:04:07.390 --> 00:04:10.140
was just to buy some 
temporary peace of mind.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:15.520
Um, is there a way to fight them?

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:19.440
At the present time, there is not.

00:04:19.830 --> 00:04:22.190
Then if we encounter our 
counterpart card...

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:24.030
Please flee.

00:04:25.870 --> 00:04:28.320
This is not a request as 
the organization's leader,

00:04:28.320 --> 00:04:29.870
but my own personal request.

00:04:30.470 --> 00:04:31.700
Because...

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:34.750
Because I don't want 
anyone to disappear.

00:04:41.980 --> 00:04:43.720
Flee, huh?

00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:48.660
I want to fight, even if it 
means that I'll disappear.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:50.640
No! Don't say that!

00:04:50.940 --> 00:04:51.970
Why?

00:04:52.460 --> 00:04:56.060
We exist for the purpose 
of fighting Daemonia.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:57.900
What about you, Luna?

00:05:00.460 --> 00:05:01.600
I...

00:05:02.100 --> 00:05:05.400
I don't want to run away 
in the face of the enemy.

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:09.890
I definitely don't want this.

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:12.650
I don't know if it's the 
counterpart card or whatever,

00:05:12.650 --> 00:05:16.040
but I don't want my life to end 
because of something like that.

00:05:16.230 --> 00:05:18.380
Then you'd run away, Ginka?

00:05:18.380 --> 00:05:19.630
Heck yes.

00:05:19.630 --> 00:05:23.550
It's only natural for humans to 
run if their lives are in danger.

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:27.050
I believe that's true, in 
a way. I won't deny it.

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:30.440
Right? If you were to disappear, 
you wouldn't be able

00:05:30.440 --> 00:05:31.810
to eat chicken salad anymore.

00:05:33.170 --> 00:05:34.390
I don't want that.

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:37.100
Apparently that was a major point.

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:49.450
That was a bit emotional.

00:05:51.360 --> 00:05:53.030
Couldn't you have explained

00:05:53.030 --> 00:05:56.040
the matter more rationally, 
as the head of the organization?

00:05:56.040 --> 00:06:00.290
The Leguzario have no right to 
tell me how I should handle this.

00:06:03.350 --> 00:06:05.850
You knew, didn't you?

00:06:06.700 --> 00:06:09.020
That the counterpart cards existed...

00:06:10.680 --> 00:06:13.430
We are only pawns ourselves.

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:21.940
<i>I wonder what I'm supposed to do.</i>

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:33.210
<i>At that moment, I put my life...</i>

00:06:35.760 --> 00:06:38.370
It's Luna. Are you busy?

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:42.230
I'm sorry for coming so suddenly.

00:06:42.230 --> 00:06:44.330
It's okay. What's wrong?

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:47.520
When I started thinking 
about the counterpart cards,

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:49.780
I got scared being by myself.

00:06:50.440 --> 00:06:54.020
I see... Actually, I was 
feeling the same way.

00:06:54.570 --> 00:06:57.870
If I were to meet the counterpart 
card to The Sun...

00:06:58.350 --> 00:07:01.420
I was wondering if I'd 
be able to fight them.

00:07:04.260 --> 00:07:05.520
I don't want you to disappear.

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:10.530
I never want you to 
disappear, Akari-san.

00:07:11.290 --> 00:07:13.130
Even if someone else,

00:07:13.130 --> 00:07:16.040
even myself, disappeared... 
If it was to protect you, I...

00:07:16.810 --> 00:07:19.040
Luna-chan?

00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:23.040
I-I'm sorry, I...

00:07:23.290 --> 00:07:26.800
It's okay. It is pretty scary.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:30.550
But I think Seira has a point, too.

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:35.560
We have our powers to 
fight the Daemonia.

00:07:35.920 --> 00:07:39.600
I was thinking that we 
do have to accept that.

00:07:48.680 --> 00:07:52.540
<i>But I think Seira has a point, too.</i>

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:57.620
Oh...

00:07:58.920 --> 00:08:00.740
Are you done with your training?

00:08:00.740 --> 00:08:01.620
Yeah.

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:05.630
Thanks for your hard 
work at this late hour.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:08.360
Thanks. Good night.

00:08:15.130 --> 00:08:17.370
Representative, may we have a comment 
on the reform within the party?

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:19.700
Please let us know.

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:25.360
Well, I'm personally sick of the 
fight for power within the party.

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:27.760
The citizens don't want that.

00:08:28.220 --> 00:08:30.010
We, the ruling party, 
shouldn't concentrate on

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:33.860
preconceived ideas about 
employment, economy, or diplomacy,

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:38.110
but should strive for a daring reform.

00:08:38.320 --> 00:08:39.120
Look out!

00:08:43.120 --> 00:08:51.880
Window Cleaning Gondola Falling Accident: 
Representative and Reporters Killed!

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:45.970
This afternoon, vice chief secretary 
of the government ruling party,

00:08:45.970 --> 00:08:47.880
Representative Nakazawa Takahiko, and

00:08:47.880 --> 00:08:51.650
five reporters who were interviewing 
him were killed after they

00:08:51.650 --> 00:08:53.570
were crushed by a gondola 
at the Teito Plaza Hotel.

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:57.550
Representative
5 People

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:57.550
Dead

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:57.550
Government Ruling Party
 Vice Chief Secretary
Nakazawa Takahiko
Reporters

00:08:53.570 --> 00:08:57.020
They were immediately taken to the 
hospital, but died shortly after.

00:08:59.520 --> 00:09:01.640
Don't do anything too flashy.

00:09:02.130 --> 00:09:03.300
Flashy?

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:05.390
That was pretty dull, if you ask me.

00:09:05.860 --> 00:09:08.400
I just said to make sure that they lose.

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:11.980
You know you wanted me to kill them.

00:09:12.220 --> 00:09:15.740
Why don't you give up that 
form already, Cerebrum?

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:20.740
You're too needy, Mister.

00:09:24.150 --> 00:09:26.380
Pretty handsome, aren't I?

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:28.750
I wouldn't say something like that.

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:30.550
I know that.

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:34.760
It doesn't feel very good 
to talk to your clone.

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:37.760
I was thinking the same thing myself.

00:09:38.930 --> 00:09:41.540
That's why I'm thinking that

00:09:41.540 --> 00:09:44.520
when I return to Nagataki, I'm going 
to let these feelings loose.

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:48.520
On the Elemental user 
you mentioned before?

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:53.290
Yeah. I found out something 
interesting the other day,

00:09:53.290 --> 00:09:55.530
so I was thinking about exploiting that.

00:09:55.940 --> 00:09:59.280
Don't do anything that'll 
threaten my position.

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:01.620
At this point?

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:04.040
You and I share the same fate.

00:10:06.320 --> 00:10:11.040
I want her no matter what. 
The child of The Sun...

00:10:55.670 --> 00:10:57.210
<i>What is this noise?</i>

00:10:58.030 --> 00:10:59.840
<i>I can't hear its voice at all.</i>

00:11:00.170 --> 00:11:00.970
What's it saying?

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:03.450
There's noise coming 
from somewhere else.

00:11:03.840 --> 00:11:07.930
Since you can't hear its voice, 
the only thing we can do is...

00:11:08.230 --> 00:11:09.180
Exterminate it!

00:11:24.270 --> 00:11:25.160
Akari-san!

00:11:38.670 --> 00:11:39.510
Not good!

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:52.830
Ginka-san!

00:11:52.100 --> 00:11:52.830
Ginka!

00:11:54.150 --> 00:11:55.270
What's going on?!

00:12:06.130 --> 00:12:07.030
Once more!

00:12:07.030 --> 00:12:08.080
Wait, Seira!

00:12:14.110 --> 00:12:14.830
Ginka-san!

00:12:18.880 --> 00:12:19.970
Ginka-san!

00:12:43.630 --> 00:12:45.740
Ginka?

00:12:46.120 --> 00:12:48.490
Could this be...

00:12:55.240 --> 00:12:58.750
It's Temperance's 
counterpart card.

00:13:08.830 --> 00:13:10.760
Now... Eternal...

00:13:10.760 --> 00:13:12.520
Huh? What?

00:13:14.520 --> 00:13:15.410
Akari!

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:23.610
No... Ginka will be hurt.

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:36.790
Ginka!

00:13:38.970 --> 00:13:40.420
Why are you holding back?

00:13:40.650 --> 00:13:41.420
But...

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:43.500
Let's run while we can! Please!

00:13:48.740 --> 00:13:50.680
Hopefully it goes well next time.

00:13:51.430 --> 00:13:54.180
If that happens, you'll 
get your wish.

00:14:00.780 --> 00:14:03.900
To think that they 
encountered one so soon.

00:14:06.100 --> 00:14:10.070
Our attacks had no effect at all.

00:14:10.070 --> 00:14:13.330
Not only that, all of the 
damage went to Ginka.

00:14:16.600 --> 00:14:20.150
We're going to examine the attack 
patterns and look for weak points.

00:14:20.150 --> 00:14:24.200
Until then, we think it's better 
that Ginka-oneetan isn't sent out.

00:14:24.200 --> 00:14:25.130
Out.

00:14:25.430 --> 00:14:26.770
Indeed.

00:14:26.770 --> 00:14:28.160
We're counting on you.

00:14:37.260 --> 00:14:40.020
Man, it's so relaxing 
not being sent out.

00:14:41.460 --> 00:14:44.010
Why are you guys the ones 
that look so bummed out?

00:14:44.010 --> 00:14:46.030
It's not going to keep 
attacking like that.

00:14:46.580 --> 00:14:50.340
Seira's attack was awesome. 
It hurt pretty bad!

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:52.480
I would have totally 
died if you had kept going.

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:54.380
It was a good thing we ran.

00:14:56.040 --> 00:14:58.160
Oh, don't have any weird regrets.

00:14:58.160 --> 00:15:00.790
Y'all didn't know the 
damage would come to me,

00:15:00.790 --> 00:15:03.620
and I'm better because of Luna.

00:15:04.910 --> 00:15:06.900
You're not scared, Ginka-san?

00:15:06.900 --> 00:15:10.300
Scared? Hm, well...

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:13.050
I'm scared, but I'm intrigued.

00:15:13.510 --> 00:15:14.560
Intrigued?

00:15:14.560 --> 00:15:18.080
Yeah. My other self was 
pretty neat, wasn't it?

00:15:18.640 --> 00:15:21.810
Well, if I don't look at it that 
way, it'd be hard to go on.

00:15:27.670 --> 00:15:29.460
I wonder if we'll be 
able to run away.

00:15:30.580 --> 00:15:32.410
Ginka, and the rest of us...

00:15:32.410 --> 00:15:35.330
We might all have to disappear some day.

00:15:38.020 --> 00:15:40.230
You're not scared, Seira?

00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:41.750
There's no point in thinking about it.

00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:44.660
Everyone dies someday.

00:15:45.110 --> 00:15:47.840
Until then, I think all that we can 
do is face what's right in front of us.

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:50.140
Yeah...

00:15:56.640 --> 00:15:58.390
<i>The Temperance card?</i>

00:15:59.210 --> 00:16:01.390
<i>Yes. This card</i>

00:16:02.100 --> 00:16:03.650
<i>is the card of balance.</i>

00:16:04.160 --> 00:16:05.400
<i>Balance?</i>

00:16:05.400 --> 00:16:07.920
<i>People will cry and get angry,</i>

00:16:07.920 --> 00:16:09.740
<i>but at times like that,</i>

00:16:09.740 --> 00:16:14.120
<i>they still need to take a 
moment to calm themselves.</i>

00:16:14.530 --> 00:16:17.350
<i>To be able to use your 
personality to the fullest...</i>

00:16:17.720 --> 00:16:20.660
<i>It symbolizes that power.</i>

00:16:21.320 --> 00:16:23.900
<i>You will most likely awaken</i>

00:16:23.900 --> 00:16:26.670
<i>right before you turn thirteen, 
just like I did, Ginka.</i>

00:16:26.910 --> 00:16:31.000
<i>That fate is hard, sad, and lonely.</i>

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:33.180
<i>You may end up hating yourself.</i>

00:16:35.050 --> 00:16:37.840
<i>But there's no need for that.</i>

00:16:37.840 --> 00:16:40.430
<i>Be proud and use your power.</i>

00:16:40.730 --> 00:16:41.750
<i>Okay.</i>

00:16:43.770 --> 00:16:47.410
I wonder what Grand Auntie 
would say if she were alive.

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:50.440
<b>Sancho Panza</b>

00:16:49.690 --> 00:16:50.840
Well, it sure is rare

00:16:50.840 --> 00:16:52.640
for you to come all 
the way to the shop.

00:16:52.640 --> 00:16:56.450
Well, I suddenly got some time off, 
so it doesn't hurt to visit sometimes.

00:16:57.550 --> 00:16:58.750
Hey, Pops...

00:16:58.750 --> 00:16:59.450
What?

00:16:59.760 --> 00:17:02.530
This power I got from Grand Auntie...

00:17:02.530 --> 00:17:04.460
I wonder why I inherited it.

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:07.460
Well, that's a pretty 
tough question.

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:10.300
Unlike Seira and Akari, I 
had no feelings

00:17:10.300 --> 00:17:13.470
about exterminating the Daemonia.

00:17:13.720 --> 00:17:16.620
Even now, I don't have any.

00:17:17.770 --> 00:17:20.510
Despite everyone 
saying it's pointless,

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:23.230
Akari can hear the 
Daemonia's voices, but

00:17:23.650 --> 00:17:26.070
we were able to learn a lot from that.

00:17:26.490 --> 00:17:29.230
Seira's really strong and 
straight as an arrow.

00:17:30.890 --> 00:17:33.490
I can't live like that.

00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:36.260
Luna is quiet, but truly nice.

00:17:36.680 --> 00:17:40.510
But I wonder if I've been able 
to give something to them.

00:17:42.380 --> 00:17:45.570
Maybe what makes it great is 
that there is nothing to give.

00:17:46.410 --> 00:17:49.400
If everyone had to 
carry anger or sadness,

00:17:49.400 --> 00:17:51.480
you might not be able to see something 
that you should be able to.

00:17:52.100 --> 00:17:55.830
At times like that, you're 
able to balance everyone out,

00:17:55.830 --> 00:17:57.720
and that's probably why 
you're all doing so well.

00:17:58.770 --> 00:18:01.580
There's no reason to 
think too hard about it.

00:18:01.580 --> 00:18:04.520
You just need to do 
what you can do, Ginka.

00:18:05.950 --> 00:18:07.570
You're right.

00:18:07.570 --> 00:18:09.520
I guess there are things 
that only I can do.

00:18:10.130 --> 00:18:11.590
Thanks, Pops.

00:18:11.590 --> 00:18:13.450
What, you're going back already?

00:18:13.450 --> 00:18:15.350
Yeah. I feel better.

00:18:15.350 --> 00:18:16.530
I see.

00:18:16.880 --> 00:18:19.950
Oh, I'll be by next week with 
some more delicious presents,

00:18:19.950 --> 00:18:21.030
so look forward to it.

00:18:22.190 --> 00:18:23.710
I will.

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:36.420
I was waiting for you.

00:18:39.100 --> 00:18:42.930
If you're really my clone, 
I knew you'd come.

00:18:43.830 --> 00:18:46.930
Eternal life...

00:18:47.110 --> 00:18:50.940
I don't really understand, 
but let's get started.

00:18:58.110 --> 00:18:59.450
Why did she go alone?

00:18:59.450 --> 00:19:00.960
Was it for us?

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:02.800
Probably. But...

00:19:03.800 --> 00:19:07.580
I think she wanted to 
fight with her own fate.

00:19:07.580 --> 00:19:10.960
But she can't! We have 
to hurry and save her.

00:19:13.070 --> 00:19:15.800
How's this?

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:30.810
Things are just starting 
to get interesting!

00:19:31.150 --> 00:19:33.810
I won't disappear.

00:19:33.810 --> 00:19:35.860
Guess we'll have to see about that.

00:19:43.330 --> 00:19:44.070
Ginka!

00:19:45.510 --> 00:19:47.080
Ginka, don't!

00:19:47.080 --> 00:19:51.080
Oh, so you've come to 
see my final battle?

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:52.150
Ginka-san!

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:54.600
Let's go back, Ginka! Hurry!

00:19:56.290 --> 00:19:57.750
Don't get in my way.

00:19:58.600 --> 00:20:00.970
This is my battle!

00:20:01.990 --> 00:20:04.970
I'm the only one that can defeat it.

00:20:04.970 --> 00:20:07.010
And if I defeat this...

00:20:07.010 --> 00:20:10.540
We'll be able to exterminate 
the Temperance Daemonia.

00:20:10.540 --> 00:20:12.230
We'll gain from a loss!

00:20:12.500 --> 00:20:13.480
But...

00:20:14.140 --> 00:20:16.730
I can't stop Ginka.

00:20:18.320 --> 00:20:20.990
If that's the path Ginka 
wants to go down...

00:20:20.990 --> 00:20:23.200
Make sure you watch my fight carefully!

00:20:25.750 --> 00:20:28.030
We're one and the same.

00:20:28.030 --> 00:20:29.750
I'll have you disappear along with me!

00:20:30.020 --> 00:20:34.750
I will not disappear. 
I'll combine with you.

00:20:34.970 --> 00:20:38.600
I'm never... going to combine with you!

00:20:42.460 --> 00:20:43.510
Ginka!

00:20:54.140 --> 00:20:57.150
Stop! Stop already!

00:20:57.580 --> 00:21:03.150
You idiot. I can't stop 
after coming this far!

00:21:03.860 --> 00:21:06.160
I will... combine with you.

00:21:06.580 --> 00:21:09.140
Here I go!

00:21:54.790 --> 00:21:55.790
Ginka...

00:22:02.580 --> 00:22:04.800
Ginka... Ginka...

00:22:06.310 --> 00:22:07.380
Ginka...

00:22:09.630 --> 00:22:14.570
Ginka!

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:29.380
<b>The moon changes itself into the 
full moon, new moon, and lunar 
eclipse depending on its phase.</b>

00:23:26.380 --> 00:23:42.380
<b>#18 The Moon</b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:30.550
Etia, I know what your hobby is.

00:23:29.380 --> 00:23:32.380
<b>The Moon card shows that human 
hearts are always changing, 
as well as ambiguous and unstable.</b>

00:23:30.550 --> 00:23:33.170
Don't say it. It's not something 
other people should know.

00:23:32.380 --> 00:23:36.390
<b>If you were to choose this 
card, it shows that you will be
 troubled by unstable situations, 
uneasy relations, or indecisive 
feelings.</b>

00:23:33.170 --> 00:23:35.810
What are you talking 
about? Your hobby is...

00:23:35.810 --> 00:23:36.820
You forgot?

00:23:36.390 --> 00:23:42.370
<b>If the card is reversed, it shows 
that you will be able to overcome 
an unstable or chaotic situation, 
and a future with bright possibilities 
or success with a positive outcome 
awaits you.</b>

00:23:36.820 --> 00:23:37.540
Um...

00:23:37.540 --> 00:23:38.410
Never mind.

00:23:37.890 --> 00:23:41.390
<b>The Moon's Light, the Sun's Shadow</b>

00:23:38.410 --> 00:23:39.080
Wha?

00:23:39.080 --> 00:23:40.610
See you next time!
